From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: johnnykang101 <johnny.kang101@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Mar 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 132/132] fix(install): restore /dev/tty stdin re-attach lost
 in Mar-28 release-scan rewrite

## RCA

The Mar 28 commit that fixed release scanning (equivalent to patch 0032)
was authored against the pre-0023 version of install.sh. Patches 0023,
0038, 0039, 0040 had progressively refined a /dev/tty stdin fix for the
`curl | bash` onboard flow, but the Mar 28 direct edit to install.sh
was based on an older baseline that predated those fixes.

**Root cause:** Direct edits to install.sh bypass the patch chain. When
a direct edit rewrites a section, any intervening patches in the chain
that touched the same section are silently lost.

**Symptom:** Arrow keys in the provider-selection prompt print as raw
escape sequences (`^[[A`, `^[[B`) because @clack/prompts can't enter raw
mode when stdin is a pipe (as it is in `curl | bash`).

## Fix

Restore the `stty </dev/tty` guard (final form from patch 0040) around
the `cobuilder onboard` call:
- stdin is a TTY  → run directly
- /dev/tty works  → redirect stdin from /dev/tty
- headless/CI     → print manual instructions

`stty` is used (not `true </dev/tty`) because the latter succeeds even
when the device is non-functional — stty actually interrogates terminal
attributes and fails correctly in headless containers.

## Prevention

Any future rewrite of install.sh MUST verify that the /dev/tty onboard
block is present. The CI e2e test (test-e2e.sh) covers the `curl | bash`
path and will catch regressions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 install.sh | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/install.sh b/install.sh
index <old>..<new> 100755
--- a/install.sh
+++ b/install.sh
@@ -141,4 +141,15 @@ echo ""
 # ── Onboard ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-"$COBUILDER_BIN" onboard
+# When piped via `curl | bash`, stdin is not a TTY — re-attach to /dev/tty
+# so interactive prompts (arrow keys etc.) work seamlessly.
+# Use `stty` (not a plain redirect) because `true </dev/tty` succeeds even
+# in headless containers where reads would fail.
+if [ -t 0 ]; then
+  "$COBUILDER_BIN" onboard
+elif (stty </dev/tty) 2>/dev/null; then
+  "$COBUILDER_BIN" onboard </dev/tty
+else
+  echo ""
+  echo -e "  ${bold}Run this to complete setup:${reset}"
+  echo -e "  ${bold}${green}cobuilder onboard${reset}"
+  echo ""
+fi
